<title>JAPAN: Japan 10-year JGB auction lowest price at 100.15.</title>
<headline>Japan 10-year JGB auction lowest price at 100.15.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Finance Ministry said the results of its auction of 2.9 percent 190th 10-year Japanese government bonds (JGB) on Wednesday, covering 60 percent of the one trillion yen issue, were as follows:</p>
<p> Lowest price	 100.15   Stop rate     2.880 pct</p>
<p> Average price	100.19   Average yield 2.875 pct</p>
<p> Total bids	   1.9407 trillion yen</p>
<p> Accepted bids	590.7 billion yen</p>
<p> Bid to cover ratio		3.29 times</p>
<p> Bids accepted at lowest price 95.9051 pct  Issue date   Oct 21, 1996   Maturity   Dec 20, 2006</p>
</text>
